<h1 focusTitle>Help</h1><div class="row text-large"><div class="col-md-7"><section><h2>Contact</h2><p>For all inquiries please send an email to <b>{{contactEmail}}</b></p></section><section><h2>Controls</h2><ul class="spaced-list"><li><b>movement</b><div class="pl-2 mb-1">Use
<kbd-key title="up arrow key"><fa-icon [icon]="upIcon"></fa-icon></kbd-key>
<kbd-key title="left arrow key"><fa-icon [icon]="leftIcon"></fa-icon></kbd-key>
<kbd-key title="down arrow key"><fa-icon [icon]="downIcon"></fa-icon></kbd-key>
<kbd-key title="right arrow key"><fa-icon [icon]="rightIcon"></fa-icon></kbd-key>
,
<kbd-key title="W key">W</kbd-key>
<kbd-key title="A key">A</kbd-key>
<kbd-key title="S key">S</kbd-key>
<kbd-key title="D key">D</kbd-key>
,
<kbd-key class="gamepad gamepad-stick" title="Gamepad left stick">L<div class="t"></div><div class="l"></div><div class="r"></div><div class="b"></div></kbd-key>
or <b>touch and drag</b> to move.
<br>
Hold <kbd-key title="shift key">shift</kbd-key> to walk slowly.</div></li><li><b>chat</b><div class="pl-2 mb-1">Use <kbd-key title="enter key">enter</kbd-key>
or <kbd-key class="gamepad gamepad-blue" title="Gamepad X button">X</kbd-key>
to open chat box and send a message.
<br>
Use <kbd-key title="escape key">esc</kbd-key>
or <kbd-key class="gamepad gamepad-blue" title="Gamepad X button">X</kbd-key>
to cancel the message.</div></li><li>hold <kbd-key title="shift key">shift</kbd-key> to be able to click on ground and items behind other players</li><li><b>boop</b> - 
<kbd-key title="B key">B</kbd-key> ,
<kbd-key class="gamepad gamepad-red" title="Gamepad B button">B</kbd-key> ,
<b>two finger tap</b>
or <code>/boop</code> command</li><li><b>interact</b> or <b>use item</b> - <kbd-key title="E key">E</kbd-key> or
<kbd-key class="gamepad gamepad-green" title="Gamepad A button">A</kbd-key></li><li><b>land</b>  or <b>sit down</b> or <b>lie down</b> - 
<kbd-key title="X key">X</kbd-key> ,
<kbd-key class="gamepad gamepad-dpad" title="Gamepad dpad down button"><div class="dpad-down"></div></kbd-key>
or <code>/stand</code> and <code>/sit</code> and <code>/lie</code> commands</li><li><b>sit up</b> or <b>stand up</b> or <b>fly up</b> - 
<kbd-key title="C key">C</kbd-key> ,
<kbd-key class="gamepad gamepad-dpad" title="Gamepad dpad up button"><div class="dpad-up"></div></kbd-key>
or <code>/sit</code> and <code>/stand</code> and <code>/fly</code> commands</li><li><b>turn head</b> - 
<kbd-key title="H key">H</kbd-key>
or <kbd-key class="gamepad gamepad-stick" title="Gamepad right stick">R<div class="t"></div><div class="l"></div><div class="r"></div><div class="b"></div></kbd-key>
or <code>/turn</code> command</li><li><b>zoom in / out</b> -
<kbd-key title="P key">P</kbd-key> and <kbd-key title="O key">O</kbd-key>
or <kbd-key class="gamepad gamepad-yellow" title="Gamepad Y button">Y</kbd-key></li><li><b>hide all text</b> -
<kbd-key title="F2 key">F2</kbd-key></li><li><b>hide public chat</b> -
<kbd-key title="F3 key">F3</kbd-key></li><li><b>see through objects</b> -
<kbd-key title="F4 key">F4</kbd-key></li><li><b>fullscreen</b> - <span *ngIf="!mac"><kbd-key title="F11 key">F11</kbd-key></span><span *ngIf="mac"><kbd-key title="Control key">ctrl</kbd-key> + <kbd-key title="command key">⌘</kbd-key> + <kbd-key title="F key">F</kbd-key></span></li></ul></section><section><h2>Expressions</h2><p>To change your pony face expression in game:</p><ul class="spaced-list"><li>type any emote in the chat <code>:)</code></li><li>end your message with an emote <code>Hey there :D</code></li><li>change expression <b>without saying</b> anything, by writing the emote as a chat command <code>/:D</code></li><li>make the expression permanent using <code>/e :(</code> command and use <code>/e</code> to get your default expression back</li><li>use both horizontal and vertical emotes: <code>&gt;:(</code> <code>D:</code> <code>O_o</code> <code>^c^</code> <code>6.9</code></li><li>use emotes with blushies like <code>O//O</code> or <code>O//v//O</code></li></ul></section><section><h2>Chat commands</h2><p>Following chat commands are available in the game chat:</p><ul class="spaced-list"><li><code>/help</code>, <code>/h</code> or <code>/?</code> - list all available commands</li><li><code>/roll</code>, <code>/rand</code> or <code>/random</code> - roll a random number between 1 and 100<ul class="spaced-list"><li>use <code>/roll 10</code> to roll a number between 1 and 10</li><li>use <code>/roll 5-10</code> to roll a number between 5 and 10</li></ul></li><li><code>/say</code> or <code>/s</code> - say in public chat (can be used to switch from party chat)</li><li><code>/party</code> or <code>/p</code> - say in party chat</li><li><code>/think</code> or <code>/t</code> - say in thinking bubble</li><li><code>/whisper &lt;name&gt;</code> or <code>/w &lt;name&gt;</code> - whisper to player (you can also click on player name in chatlog)</li><li><code>/reply</code> or <code>/r</code> - reply to last incoming whisper</li><li><code>/e</code> - set a permanent expression like this <code>/e :)</code></li><li><code>/unstuck</code> - resets position to spawn point and leaves the game</li><li><code>/leave</code> - leaves the game</li><li><code>/turn</code> - turn head around</li><li><code>/magic</code> - toggle magic light</li><li><code>/drop</code> - drop held item</li><li><code>/droptoy</code> - drop held toy</li><li><code>/open</code> - open gift</li><li><code>/toys</code> - show number of collected toys</li><li><code>/boop</code> or <code>/)</code> - do a boop. Can also be used with expression: <code>/) XD</code></li><li><code>/lie</code> - lie down or sit up</li><li><code>/sit</code> - sit down or stand up</li><li><code>/stand</code> - stand up or land</li><li><code>/fly</code> - fly up or land</li><li><code>/sleep</code> or <code>/zzz</code> - fall asleep. Can also be used with some expressions: <code>/zzz :)</code></li><li><code>/love</code> or <code>/&lt;3</code> - show floating hearts. Can also be used with expressions: <code>/love :)</code></li><li><code>/cry</code> - start crying. Can also be used with expressions: <code>/cry :D</code></li><li><code>/blush</code> - start blushing. Can also be used with expressions: <code>/blush :D</code></li><li>Following expression commands are available:
<code>/smile</code> <code>/happy</code>
<code>/frown</code>
<code>/angry</code>
<code>/sad</code>
<code>/thinking</code>
<code>/yawn</code>
<code>/laugh</code> <code>/haha</code> <code>/хаха</code> <code>/jaja</code> <code>/lol</code>
<code>/sneeze</code> <code>/achoo</code></li><li><strong>House saving</strong><ul><li><code>/savehouse</code> - saves current house setup (single save state for entire account)</li><li><code>/loadhouse</code> - loads saved house setup (need to be alone in the house or a party leader)</li><li><code>/resethouse</code> - resets house setup to original state (need to be alone in the house or a party leader)</li><li><code>/lockhouse</code> - prevents other people from changing the house (need to be alone in the house or a party leader)</li><li><code>/unlockhouse</code> - enables editing by other people (need to be alone in the house or a party leader)</li><li><code>/removetoolbox</code> - removes toolbox from the house (need to be alone in the house or a party leader)</li><li><code>/restoretoolbox</code> - restores toolbox to the house (need to be alone in the house or a party leader)</li></ul></li></ul></section><section><h4>Supporter-only commands</h4><ul class="spaced-list"><li><code>/ss</code> - supporter colored text</li><li><code>/s1</code> - tier 1 supporter colored text (for use by higher tier supporters)</li><li><code>/s2</code> - tier 2 supporter colored text (for use by higher tier supporters)</li><li><code>/s3</code> - tier 3 supporter colored text (for use by higher tier supporters)</li></ul></section><section><h2>Chat emojis</h2><p>You can use emojis in chat by typing their name surrounded by colons <samp>:apple:</samp>
or by using unicode characters assigned to them. Available emotes:
</p><div class="emotes"><ul><li *ngFor="let e of emotes"><span class="emote-sample mr-2"><emote-box [emote]="e"></emote-box></span>:{{e}}:</li></ul></div></section></div><div class="col-md-5"><section><h2>Common issues</h2><section><h4>Keys stuck when using iPad keyboard</h4><p class="text-fading">Due to a bug on iOS system some keys will get stuck occasionally,
when the key gets stuck just press it again to unstuck it.</p><p class="text-fading">We recommend you use arrow keys for movement as those keys do not get stuck.
</p></section><section><h4>Other players can't see my messages</h4><p class="text-fading">This happens when you get temporarily muted for breaking the rules.
This typically takes from a few hours to a few days depending on severity and frequency of the violation.</p><p class="text-fading">Avoid breaking the rules to prevent this from happening in the future.
</p></section><section><h4>Page not loading or stuck updating</h4><p class="text-fading">Try reloading and clearing your browser data.
If that doesn't help you should check if any of the extensions are causing the issue,
you can check that by using incognito mode of your browser.
</p></section><section><h4>Mobile keyboard is covering the chat box when the game is installed on mobile device</h4><p class="text-fading">Try re-installing the game.
</p></section><section><h4>Screen black or blinking after joining the game</h4><p class="text-fading">This is usually caused by outdated graphics drivers or browser.
Check if your browser is <a href="https://updatemybrowser.org/">up to date</a> and check
if there are new updates for your graphics card or device.</p><p class="text-fading">If your browser is already up to date, try installing different browser.
We recommend using <a href="https://www.google.com/chrome/">Chrome</a>
or <a href="https://www.mozilla.org/en-US/firefox/new/">Firefox</a>.</p><p class="text-fading">Some older devices don't support necessary functions and will never work with the game.
</p></section><section><h4>Graphical glitches, disappearing objects</h4><p class="text-fading">This can be caused by outdated drivers or not enough graphics memory,
see previous points for possible solutions.
</p></section><section><h4>Cannot connect to the game</h4><p class="text-fading">This can be caused by outdated browser or network issues.
Try updating your browser or installing a different one, see previous points for more info.</p><p class="text-fading">Connection issue might also be a result of our DDOS protection service,
reloading the page and trying again should solve the issue in that case.
</p></section><section><h4>Game slow or stuttering</h4><p class="text-fading">This can be caused by outdated browser or some browser extensions.</p><p class="text-fading">Adblock extension on <b>Chrome</b> browser is known to cause stuttering in the game,
make sure to disable it to avoid any issues. Other similar extensions may also cause
slowdowns and stuttering in the game.</p><p class="text-fading">Firefox is known to have issues with stuttering, we recommend
using <b>Chrome</b> or <b>Edge</b> browsers for best performance.
</p></section><section><h4>Why can't I create multiple accounts</h4><p class="text-fading">This restriction is in-place to protect you and the game itself from other players in the game.</p><p class="text-fading">Allowing multiple accounts for single person invalidates ignore and hide systems that 
allow you to ignore and hide other players that are harassing or bothering you in any way.
It also invalidates mute and ban system that is in-place to protect you from players breaking
the game rules to bother or harass others.</p><p class="text-fading">Allowing use of multiple accounts at the same time would dramatically increase load on the
server and potentially make the game unplayable and laggy for everyone else. Increased amount
of player characters in the game would also reduce rendering performance on slower computers,
especially on mobile devices to the point when a lot of players wouldn't be able to play the
game anymore.</p><p class="text-fading">Use of multiple accounts also invalidates any limits (like character limit) that we put on the accounts.
The limits are in-place to prevent large amount of players that we have at the moment from
exhausting our limited server resources.
</p></section><section><h4>Why can't I modify the game with hacks or scripts</h4><p class="text-fading">This restriction is in-place to protect you and the game itself from other players in the game.</p><p class="text-fading">Almost all third-party scripts used in-game were used to harass other players. Even when the
creator of the script did not intend it to be used in that way, the limited knowledge of the
game and security issues can lead to unintentionally creating a script that's harmful to other
players in the game.</p><p class="text-fading">Even in the case where the script doesn't seem to impact other players, it often causes performance
issues for the server or other players. That forces us to work on putting more limits on player
interactions and takes development time away from adding new features to the game.</p><p class="text-fading">Adding more limits on player interactions also makes the game less responsive and more limiting
for everyone, not only the players using scripts. This is especially bad for players on bad
internet connections where network issues can be misinterpreted as use of scripts or spam.
</p></section></section></div></div><div class="text-center text-muted mt-3"><div class="tinyface"></div></div>